The detector description layer with libc++ and on macOS:
- TrkParametersBase: CxxUtils::sincos (ATLAS's portable one) rather than sincos(), a GNU
  extension;
- includes that libstdc++ brings in through other headers and libc++ does not (<sstream>,
  <iterator>, <vector>, <iomanip>, <ostream>), and none of libstdc++'s own
  <ext/alloc_traits.h>;
- MdtCalibData: the Legendre polynomials by their recurrence with libc++, which has no special
  mathematical functions (std::legendre);
- ITkPixelOnlineId: hashed through its own conversion (to unsigned long), not to uint64_t,
  which is unsigned long long on macOS;
- MuonStation: std::setiosflags qualified (libstdc++ finds it by argument-dependent lookup);
- ActsGeometry's ExtrapolationTool: prepareOptions<>() defined before its uses, in lambdas that
  std::visit instantiates (clang emitted none of its instantiations otherwise);
- TRT_GeoModel: GeoModel's GeoGenfun::ArrayFunction rather than its own copy of the class (an
  ODR violation: on macOS the copy's RTTI differs from GeoModel's, and GeoModel's writer could
  not persistify the TRT's straw functions).

